# Python
[% if 'python' in languages %]

The example application imports the shared `example_core` library. Both use a
`src` layout and share this directory's `uv.lock`; the library ships `py.typed`.
The sample package identifiers are stable so the complete lock is reusable.
Rename them together with their imports and regenerate the lock when adopting
your own domain vocabulary.

Run from the repository root:

```bash
just python::setup
just python::run Ada
just python::check
```

`setup` installs locked dependencies. Ordinary checks use the local environment
and cache. Add libraries under `packages/` and executable applications under
`apps/`, then explicitly run `uv lock` here and commit the updated manifest and
lock. `just python::build` writes wheels and source archives to ignored `dist/`.

The pinned Nix environment supplies native Ruff and Pyrefly executables. Ruff
checks style, Pyrefly checks types, and the uv environment supplies pytest to
exercise the library and real application entry point. See
[ARCHITECTURE.md](ARCHITECTURE.md) for ownership.
[% endif %]
[% if agents %]

## Repository scripts

AgentSync's collision preflight is a zero-dependency PEP 723 script under
scripts/agent_preflight/. Its interpreter comes from Nix; it does not require the
Python application workspace. Run it through the root agents commands.
[% endif %]
[% if workflows %]

## Workflow scripts

Planning and reference commands use scripts/workflow/script.py with its own
PEP 723 metadata and sidecar lock. It runs independently of the application
workspace; use the root creation, sync and check commands.
[% endif %]
